{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/842681-confirm-this-to-me","id":842681,"title":"Confirm this to me...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-05T12:29:19-08:00","id":842681,"title":"Confirm this to me...","content":"Basically a changeling is someone which can see himself as a noble elf in a shining mithril armor.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to mundane eyes he's just a stupid man wrapped in some silver paper.<br /> <br /> Please tell me I'm missing something!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T13:26:15-08:00","id":842702,"title":"","content":"You're missing enchantment, Calling Upon the Wyrd, and Wyrd cantrips, among other things. Enchantment allows a changeling to bring a mortal into the fae world, letting them see what changelings see. Calling Upon the Wyrd allows a changeling to make their fae self manifest in the material world. Wyrd cantrips are fae magic that has obvious real-world effects.<br /> <br /> However, if someone who's unenchanted witnesses something fae, the Mists set in, and their memory of what happened is likely to get clouded.<br /> <br /> Basically, while a changeling might look to ordinary people like someone who's delusional, they really do have access to a world most humans can't see, and they can show them the reality of that world, even if only for a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T11:26:31-08:00","id":843058,"title":"","content":"You're missing the part where being an &quot;noble elf in shining mithril armor&quot; is just as real as &quot;the stupid man in some silver paper&quot; even if normal humans can't see or interact with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T09:16:54-08:00","id":843471,"title":"","content":"To be fair to the OP, it can be difficult to make the reality of the &quot;noble elf in mithril armor&quot; actually matter to those who can't perceive it. It can be done, but it's not as well supported as it should be by the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T10:53:49-08:00","id":843519,"title":"","content":"What's so hard about spending a point of Glamour and a point of WP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T12:51:09-08:00","id":843575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/842681-confirm-this-to-me?p=843519#post843519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's so hard about spending a point of Glamour and a point of WP?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doing so and getting them back before the Chronicle is over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T16:27:54-08:00","id":843667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/842681-confirm-this-to-me?p=843575#post843575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doing so and getting them back before the Chronicle is over.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> hate to say it but you've kind of got a point...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T00:28:21-08:00","id":843850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/842681-confirm-this-to-me?p=843058#post843058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing the part where being an &quot;noble elf in shining mithril armor&quot; is just as real as &quot;the stupid man in some silver paper&quot; even if normal humans can't see or interact with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the key. A changeling isn't some deluded lunatic . . . .well, not usually. He (or she) is a faerie creature &quot;wearing&quot; a human body to survive in the hostile modern world. And that means they exist on two levels of reality at the same time - mundane reality and fairy tale realm. If you're familiar with <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b>, its roughly equivalent to being on Earth and in the Umbra at the same time - and having to cope with events in both simultaneously.<br /> <br /> So yeah, some of the precautions they have to take might look odd/goofy/insane to a mundane human. The mundane human, though, doesn't have to cope with a pissed off dragon, or a nightmarishly huge spider trying to lay eggs in you brain. . .<br /> <br /> . . . but neither does the mundane human get to ride on the back of a unicorn, or waltz among the stars in a castle crafted of moonlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 03-08-2016, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T05:33:08-08:00","id":843907,"title":"","content":"Getting Willpower back for Changelings is as easy as anyone else 1pt per night plus points gained for following Legacies. Glamour while trickier can still be gained via Musing or Ravaging or sleeping at a freehold or you could just use Dross.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T07:46:11-08:00","id":843958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/842681-confirm-this-to-me?p=843907#post843907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting Willpower back for Changelings is as easy as anyone else 1pt per night plus points gained for following Legacies. Glamour while trickier can still be gained via Musing or Ravaging or sleeping at a freehold or you could just use Dross.</div> </div> </div> </div>Musing takes longer than many Chronicles. Ravaging is unreliable and &quot;icky,&quot; and can also take forever depending on the ST. Sleeping at a freehold's about the only way, and, like in Mage with nodes, tends to get STs in a snit if everybody has access to one, since it's supposed to be &quot;rare&quot; and &quot;special&quot; (but the mechanics make it too essential).<br /> <br /> I like Changeling, but being allowed to work magic more than once in a great while is really difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T10:05:21-08:00","id":844025,"title":"","content":"Even at a freehold, you regain a point per night in most cases, and have to get permission from whoever owns it if it's not yours. A five-dot freehold gives one point to up to 10 changelings. It's really not a lot.<br /> <br /> The Glamour economy is always a gripe of changeling players'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T04:13:00-08:00","id":844422,"title":"","content":"Ravaging should be as hard as a Wraith gaining Pathos (as its the same thing) and Dreamers background and Dross always seem hugely overlooked in the Glamour economy. The musing time tabling could do with being smaller for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T07:27:54-08:00","id":844494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/842681-confirm-this-to-me?p=844422#post844422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravaging should be as hard as a Wraith gaining Pathos (as its the same thing) and Dreamers background and Dross always seem hugely overlooked in the Glamour economy. The musing time tabling could do with being smaller for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble with even the Dreamers background is that the time it takes to Muse is just so prohibitive. You can maybe get a small infusion of glamour once every couple of months per Dreamer your background covers. To spend Glamour the way, say, a vampire spends blood or a werewolf spends gnosis (which seems to be the expected rate-of-burn, more or less, for an active magic-using Changeling), you'd need to be able to recover it as easily as a vampire does blood. A vampire can spend a few hours a night hunting to make this up. Ravaging doesn't quite live up to that. Musing certainly doesn't, not unless you have 30+ dreamers whose creations are carefully staggered so one's finishing a work every 1-2 days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T17:48:57-08:00","id":844822,"title":"","content":"Don't have books directly on hand but I'm sure there was a part of the Dreamers background that also generated Dross, which by description is abundant enough for the Changelngs to employ as a currency (but of course is consumed in use and typically only provides 1pt or 2pt of Glamour). Changelings shouldn't be sending Glamour like a Vampire spends blood as most of what a Changeling will be doing that requires Arts will typically be chimerical in nature thus bypassing much of the Glamour cost. Garou Gnosis is probably closer and that doesn't come back quick, 1pt per day from meditation otherwise you have to cut a bargain with a spirit (most do not want to surrender Gnosis) or go and engage in a sacred hunt. Effecting mortals with a chimerical cantrip also doesn't Require glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T17:55:22-08:00","id":844824,"title":"","content":"No, it's *scarce* enough to use as currency. Its value is what means it's tradeable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:57:16-07:00","id":848281,"title":"","content":"Rate of Glamour regeneration is something we're examining for C20. We want Glamour to feel scarce, sure, but there's also a certain level of &quot;well, this sucks&quot; in not being able to use your magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:06:46-07:00","id":848372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/842681-confirm-this-to-me?p=848281#post848281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rate of Glamour regeneration is something we're examining for C20. We want Glamour to feel scarce, sure, but there's also a certain level of &quot;well, this sucks&quot; in not being able to use your magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would suggest that it be handled more akin to Quintessence in Mage, then: not necessary to use magic, but when you can use it, woah nelly does it get impressive. Make it used for things like Invoke the Dragon's Ire (and make sure that's a suitably terrifying display of Faerie Might and Madness), for enchanting mortals (hey, THAT can stay something special and rare without damaging PC ability to use their magic), and maybe attach special boosts to various Arts or Realms when Glamour is applied. Those should be awe-inspiring boosts to already-useful powers, though, not ho-hum powers that become actually interesting only when Glamour is spent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T15:20:56-07:00","id":848438,"title":"","content":"I don't know, the stated themes of Changeling would seem to dictate that their powers be rather low-key and/or costly to use...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1666-firstborn8","name":"Firstborn8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T16:30:47-07:00","id":848472,"title":"","content":"Like the kithain themselves, the game is rather torn between two beings. It's partly a desperate world of holding onto the magic while everything turns cold around you. It's also partly an urban fantasy romp hidden behind closed doors and even in plain sight. These two sides to the game often compete against each other.<br /> <br /> From personal experience, I've played more urban fantasy games with Changeling than angsty ones, because I already play Vampire and Wraith.<br /> <br /> It could even be as simple as widening the options for Holdings and Dreamers, whereby one dot actually gives five points of Glamour or somesuch. This already happens with the Node background, where it can represent one point of Quintessence per level or up to five.<br /> <br /> Another is just to overhaul Musing (my favoured option). If Musing is too difficult, then players don't see it as viable, and it ironically becomes less a theme of the game because it doesn't actually get played out. <br /> <br /> Inanimae only have to meditate in an appropriate element. I'd let kithain meditate in a creative way instead (e.g., undergoing or inspiring a bout of creativity for a few hours). That would be fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T11:58:13-07:00","id":852524,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that Vampire and Wraith do the &quot;angsty, fading world&quot; better than C:tD partially because they more freely let you use your powers. Yes, things get darker, colder, and more disturbing, but you're still a supernatural thing in that darkness. C:tD needs to rethink its approach to doing the &quot;cold, fading world.&quot; I think more play on the war of their dual natures, where their human nature genuinely offers advantages (other than &quot;ignore magic&quot;) if they're willing to invoke it, would be desirable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T20:42:59-07:00","id":852783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/842681-confirm-this-to-me?p=852524#post852524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that Vampire and Wraith do the &quot;angsty, fading world&quot; better than C:tD partially because they more freely let you use your powers. Yes, things get darker, colder, and more disturbing, but you're still a supernatural thing in that darkness. C:tD needs to rethink its approach to doing the &quot;cold, fading world.&quot; I think more play on the war of their dual natures, where their human nature genuinely offers advantages (other than &quot;ignore magic&quot;) if they're willing to invoke it, would be desirable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've been a big fan of Glamour traps you in story logic, in tropes. Glamour binds you to explain your plans to your foes, to make elaborate death traps. Banality lets you just pull out a gun and shoot him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T06:26:03-07:00","id":852926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/842681-confirm-this-to-me?p=852783#post852783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've been a big fan of Glamour traps you in story logic, in tropes. Glamour binds you to explain your plans to your foes, to make elaborate death traps. Banality lets you just pull out a gun and shoot him.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has merit. It would be an interesting thing to work together with the &quot;act according to the rules of the Fae for Glamour&quot; c